# Local clone paths for the repos this knowledge base documents.
#
# Copy to `.env` and set these to wherever your own clones live. `.env` is
# gitignored; this file is the committed template.
#
# The KB and its skills refer to these repos by variable name ($WEB_REPO, ...)
# rather than by path, so moving a clone is a one-line edit here instead of a
# search-and-replace across the KB.
#
# To resolve them in a shell:
#
#     set -a; source .env; set +a
#     ls "$KB_REPO"
#
# kb-init and kb-add-project add one variable per documented repo below,
# each with a one-line comment saying what the repo is.

# The documented repos usually sit under one root; the rest derive from it.
REPOS_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/your/repos

# This knowledge base itself.
KB_REPO=${REPOS_ROOT}/kb
